"date":"19/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Select Committee Monthly Budget Report - Children Families and Education - March 2026","url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s66061/select-committee-monthly-budget-report-children-families-and.pdf","committee":"Children, Families and Education Select Committee","date":"12/03/2026","key":false},{"title":"260305 - Monthly budget and spend report","url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s65900/260305-monthly-budget-and-spend-report.pdf","committee":"Corporate Resources & Infrastructure Select Committee","date":"05/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"260226 - 08 - Budget","url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s65831/260226-08-budget.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"26/02/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit, Finance & Performance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"CABINET","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Audit, Finance & Performance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Hillingdon Standing Advisory Council on Religious Education","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"CABINET","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-24","committee":"Corporate Resources & Infrastructure Select Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Corporate Resources & Infrastructure Select Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-05","committee":"Audit, Finance & Performance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Audit, Finance & Performance Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Corporate Resources & Infrastructure Select Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Hillingdon's homelessness budget masks rising demand, council warns","lead":"Hillingdon Council started the financial year 2026/27 with 155 fewer households than budgeted in nightly-paid emergency accommodation, putting the homelessness budget on track for a \u00a33.4m underspend. But the council's month-four budget monitoring reveals a troubling reversal. Placements in the first four months increased by 11, against a budgeted reduction of 7 over the same period. The cabinet has identified a \u00a31.2m risk should this trend continue for the remainder of the year. The underlying demand for emergency housing is moving in the wrong direction, the council concluded, and the favourable variance that opened the year is closing.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"Cabinet Agenda B - Budget Monitoring","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/b15940/Cabinet Agenda B - Budget Monitoring 17th-Sep-2026 19.00 CABINET.pdf?T=9","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","paper_title":"Appendix B","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","headline":"HRA capital programme shows identical deferral pattern: \u00a33.8m underspent in 2026/27, \u00a36.5m overspent in 2027/28.","detail":"HRA approved capital of \u00a3155.9m for 2026/27 is forecast at \u00a3152.1m (\u00a33.8m variance). In 2027/28, approved \u00a3101.9m is forecast at \u00a3108.4m (\u00a36.5m variance). Key deferrals include Housing Supply Block Purchases (\u00a33.1m moved to 2027/28) and Haydon Drive development (\u00a33.5m moved to 2027/28). HRA prudential borrowing increases by \u00a36.5m in 2027/28.","category":"capital","matters":"The HRA is a separate but related account. The same deferral pattern across both General Fund and HRA suggests a systematic delivery or capacity constraint, not project-specific issues. This indicates broader programme management challenges affecting the council's ability to execute planned investment.","figures":"HRA Approved 2026/27: \u00a3155,938k; Forecast: \u00a3152,103k; Variance (\u00a33,835k). Approved 2027/28: \u00a3101,917k; Forecast: \u00a3108,431k; Variance +\u00a36,514k.","quote":"HRA Housing Supply Block Purchases a - Expenditure 28,056 -   -   0 -   25,000 3,056 -   (3,056) 3,056 -","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","paper_title":"Appendix B","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","headline":"Selected capital projects overspending while majority underspend, indicating uneven delivery.","detail":"While the overall programme is underspending, specific projects are overspending: Digital, Data and Technology Investment forecast at \u00a34.7m vs approved \u00a34.2m (+\u00a3515k); Transport for London schemes \u00a31.95m vs approved \u00a31.46m (+\u00a3491k); Carbon Initiatives \u00a31.5m vs approved \u00a3500k (+\u00a31.0m); Chrysalis Programme \u00a3428k vs approved \u00a390k (+\u00a3338k). These overspends are absorbed within the overall programme shortfall but indicate mixed project governance and priorities.","category":"capital","matters":"A finance director must understand which projects are performing within plan and which are not. Overspending on digital transformation and environmental projects while underspending on maintenance and care suggests either shifting priorities or uneven project management capability.","figures":"Digital +\u00a3515k; TfL schemes +\u00a3491k; Carbon Initiatives +\u00a31,000k; Chrysalis +\u00a3338k.","quote":"2025/26 005 Digital, Data and Technology Investment a - Expenditure  4,198 3,999 50 1,439 325 4,713 3,999 50 515 -   -","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","paper_title":"Appendix B","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","headline":"Prudential borrowing profile shifting: \u00a310.8m less in 2026/27, \u00a38.2m more in 2027/28.","detail":"General Fund prudential borrowing approved at \u00a366.5m for 2026/27 is forecast at \u00a355.7m (\u00a310.8m reduction). However, 2027/28 prudential borrowing is forecast at \u00a346.6m vs approved \u00a338.4m (\u00a38.2m increase). HRA shows similar pattern: \u00a34m less borrowing in 2026/27, \u00a36.5m more in 2027/28. Combined, borrowing across both funds is \u00a314.8m lower in 2026/27 but \u00a314.8m higher in 2027/28.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A lender needs to understand actual debt issuance timing and refinancing risk. This pattern concentrates borrowing into 2027/28, creating a peak funding year and extending the maturity profile of the council's debt portfolio. It also means less cash available in 2026/27 than planned.","figures":"GF Approved Prudential Borrow 2026/27: (\u00a366,531k); Forecast: (\u00a355,726k); Variance +\u00a310,804k. Approved 2027/28: (\u00a338,393k); Forecast: (\u00a346,636k); Variance (\u00a38,243k).","quote":"b - Prudential Borrowing (66,531) (38,393) (26,758) -   -   (55,726) (46,636) (29,758) 10,804 (8,243) (3,000)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","paper_title":"Appendix B","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","headline":"Hillingdon Water Sports Facility project significantly behind schedule, \u00a37.4m underspent in 2026/27.","detail":"Approved expenditure for the Water Sports Facility in 2026/27 was \u00a315.2m but forecast is \u00a37.8m\u2014variance of \u00a37.4m (49% underspend). Forecast 2027/28 is \u00a36.4m vs approved \u00a36.2m, indicating the \u00a37.4m is not being recovered in the next year. This suggests the project is significantly further behind schedule than a simple one-year deferral.","category":"capital","matters":"A major capital project \u00a37.4m behind schedule signals project management or delivery risk. A lender needs to understand whether the project has cost overrun risk ahead and whether it will be completed as planned. Extended timelines increase build cost risk.","figures":"Approved 2026/27: \u00a315,208k; Forecast: \u00a37,800k; Variance (\u00a37,408k); Forecast 2027/28: \u00a36,442k vs approved \u00a36,234k.","quote":"2025/26 019 Hillingdon Water Sports Facility & Activity a - Expenditure  15,208 6,234 7,000 528 3,605 7,800 6,442 6,792 (7,408) 208 (208)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"CABINET","paper_title":"Appendix B","paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","headline":"Disabled Facilities Grant programme deferring \u00a34.4m from 2026/27 to 2027/28.","detail":"Approved disabled facilities grant spending for 2026/27 was \u00a36.6m, forecast \u00a32.1m (variance \u00a34.4m). The grant-funded programme is forecast to recover in 2027/28 at \u00a36.6m. This defers statutory adaptations to disabled residents' homes.","category":"capital","matters":"Disabled facilities grants are statutory demand-driven spending. Shortfall signals either project delivery capability issues or an unexpected change in demand realisation. It also indicates the council is not responding to disability access needs at planned pace.","figures":"Approved 2026/27: \u00a36,585k; Forecast: \u00a32,146k; Variance (\u00a34,439k); Forecast 2027/28: \u00a36,585k.","quote":"2025/26 053 Disabled Facilities Grant a - Expenditure  6,585 2,146 2,146 922 346 2,146 6,585 2,146 (4,439) 4,439 -","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Hillingdon","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":true,"headline":"HRA capital programme shows identical deferral pattern: \u00a33.8m underspent in 2026/27, \u00a36.5m overspent in 2027/28.","lead":"The HRA is a separate but related account. The same deferral pattern across both General Fund and HRA suggests a systematic delivery or capacity constraint, not project-specific issues. This indicates broader programme management challenges affecting the\u2026","also":["28 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit, Finance & Performance Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":29,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix B","top_paper_url":"https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/s67468/67468.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":105,"news_drafts_total":1}}